[00:17.68]1. The meditation of my heart,
[00:22.32]The thoughts I ponder through the day—
[00:28.68]May they be pleasing to you, Lord,
[00:35.64]And keep me steadfast in your way.
[00:43.40]When worries weigh upon my mind
[00:49.76]And make me restless in the night,
[00:58.50]Then may I meditate on you
[01:04.96]And things I know to be upright.
[01:13.78]2. Whatever things are chaste and true,
[01:13.86]Whatever virtue there may be,
[01:13.88]Whatever things well-spoken-of—
[01:38.16]May thoughts of these bring peace to me.
[01:45.32]How precious are your thoughts, O God!
[01:54.94]Beyond all counting is their sum.
[02:00.02]So may I ponder your own words,
[02:07.86]Absorbed in them may I become.
